# Q: does a gun with an allied unit inside its killing range shoot at it?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --alliance-demo --probe tools/probe/alliance-demo.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/alliance-demo.txt
#
# Five tanks on open ground, in two scenes. To the south, a Σοβιετικοί tank with a Κινέζοι tank
# sixty metres from it and nothing else inside its reach at all. To the north, the same pair with a
# Δυτικοί tank a hundred metres out — so the ally is the *nearer* of the two candidates the northern
# tank has, and nothing but the side they are on can decide which of them it engages.
#
# Teams 0 and 1 are allied and team 2 is not, which `teams` prints from SimWorld.AreAllied — the same
# question every weapon asks. Each tank has five thousand hit points so that the line-up survives the
# demonstration; `units` prints the role's catalogue health after the slash, so that reads 5000/320.
#
# The standard skirmish cannot show this. On most seeds its two allied armies never come within
# weapon reach of each other at all once they stop shooting each other — the fighting that used to
# drag them together was the bug — so a probe run of a match reads a zero that could mean anything.
# This fixture puts the ally in the crosshairs and lets the zero mean what it says.

# --- the line-up, and what the world says about it -------------------------------------------------
units
teams

# --- the moment of decision ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One tick: every weapon here starts with its cooldown at zero, so after one tick each of them has
# acquired a target and fired once. `unit` prints the target it picked and the distance to it, and
# `range` prints the reach that choice was made inside.
tick 1
teams
unit 509
unit 508
unit 506
range 509

# --- a few seconds later ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The northern Σοβιετικοί tank is shooting the Δυτικοί tank a hundred metres away while its Κινέζοι
# ally stands at sixty; the Δυτικοί tank, whose nearest hostile is that ally, is shooting back at it;
# and the southern Σοβιετικοί tank, with an ally sixty metres away and no enemy in reach, holds no
# target at all.
tick 200
teams
unit 509
unit 506
events 8

# --- the ledger of measurements --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every one of these is a zero that must stay a zero: the map's allied pair is one pair, nothing aims
# at an ally while an ally is in reach, no weapon holds an ally as a target on any tick, no shot is
# fired at one, and no damage or loss goes unexplained.
expect "allied pairs on this map" 1 1 0
expect "units aiming at an ally while an ally is in reach" 0 0 0
expect "ticks with an ally held as a target" 0 0 0
expect "shots fired at an ally" 0 0 0
expect "damage no hostile weapon can account for" 0 0 0
